          %h2#references References
          %p
            The first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            was given in
          %ul
            %li#Roig94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agust%C3%AD+Roig"}> Agustí Roig
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model category structures in bifibred categories
              %strong 95
              2 (1994) 203–223 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(94)90074-4"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(94)90074-4
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            This article (
            %a{:href => "#Roig94"}> Roig 94
            ) had a mistake, which was fixed in
          %ul
            %li#Stanculesu12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+E.+Stanculescu"}> Alexandru E. Stanculescu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bifibrations and weak factorisation systems
              %strong 20
              1 (2012) 19–30 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10485-009-9214-3"}> doi:10.1007/s10485-009-9214-3
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The construction was then generalized in
          %ul
            %li#HarpazPrasma15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yonatan+Harpaz"}> Yonatan Harpaz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matan+Prasma"} Matan Prasma
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Grothendieck construction for model categories
              %strong 281
              (2015) 1306-1363 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.1852"}> arXiv:1404.1852
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2015.03.031"} 10.1016/j.aim.2015.03.031
          %p and further in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Cagne"}> Pierre Cagne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Andr%C3%A9+Melli%C3%A8s"} Paul-André Melliès
              = succeed "," do
                %em On bifibrations of model categories
              %strong 370
              (2020) 107205 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.10484"}> arXiv:1709.10484
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2020.107205"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2020.107205
          %p
            For the special case of pseudofunctors with values in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            version of the Grothendieck construction was discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sharon+Hollander"}> Sharon Hollander
              ,
              %em A homotopy theory for stacks
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0110247"}> arXiv:math.AT/0110247
              ).
